kind: graph
semantic_diff: >-
  Ten recorded graph-layer defects in one revision, every one of them prose
  inside existing structure: two checks asked the wrong question, and five node
  bodies restated duties their references pin once - one of those restatements
  carrying the wrong remedy. Counts: 32 nodes / 95 edges / 16 checks / 24
  evidence definitions / 5 control endpoints, all unchanged. Every node id,
  outcome set, role list, allowed and forbidden effect, consumes and produces
  list, required_evidence list, check style, evaluator and failure route is
  byte-identical, proved by parsing both graphs and comparing them field by
  field, not by reading the diff. No node, outcome, edge, check or evidence
  definition is added, removed or re-scoped. 28 added lines against 36 removed in
  9 hunks, a net cut of 8 lines.

  (1) THE MEASUREMENT-TRAP ACTIVITY NO LONGER PRESCRIBES THE INSTRUMENT THAT
  FAILED. realize_measurement_procedures told the measurer "the stock
  serving-benchmark path undercounts speculative-decode configurations (use a
  streaming harness for those); the decode-only bench connector produces no
  correctness signal" (:2047-2050). Its authority says the opposite about the
  remedy: the undercount comes from deriving throughput out of stream chunks in
  ANY harness, a campaign's own streaming harness reproduced it, and whether the
  stock tool shares the failure is unverified at this pin
  (references/measurement-pitfalls.md:46-50). A measurer following the activity
  builds the anti-pattern. Both clauses are now one pointer plus the clause that
  changes what the node does: realize no procedure that reproduces a trap
  recorded in references/measurement-pitfalls.md, and where a trap is in what
  the procedure counts, swapping the instrument that exposed it is not the
  remedy. WHY, generally: it names no tool, no model and no metric, and it
  corrects the reasoning error rather than the example - the graph told a seat to
  fix a mismeasurement by changing instruments, which is how the field defect
  happened. This is the acceptance ladder's own anti-backfire guard (pave-spec
  5.3.1: a metric that does not measure the acceptance property is as much a
  defect as missing evidence). Both readers of this node resolve the reference -
  the seat contract agents/measurer.md:33-37 cites it by name and the lead brief
  at SKILL.md:225 orders it read - so a multi-clause restatement here is a
  pointer under the equivalence rule. The wrong remedy is delivered revision-0
  text: it appears in no ledger patch. The release layer corrected its own copies
  at 1.5.2 and disclosed this graph copy as owed (VERSION:29, 1.5.2
  review-record residual 1, which also names the decode-connector clause cut
  here).

  (2) THE KICKOFF GATE ASKS FOR THE CONTRACT FIELD ITS DEFINER DEFINES.
  kickoff_contract_approved required a "deepseek carry-over decision" (:256).
  The node that assembles the contract calls the same field "prior-run carry-over
  decisions" (:512) and the node that surfaces it says the same (:436), and the
  check now uses that term. WHY, generally: a gate that names one campaign's
  target asks every other campaign to approve a field that does not exist for
  it, so a lead reads the clause as inapplicable and the field goes unchecked at
  the one gate that owns it - the model name made a live check unfireable on
  every run but one. No strength moves: the same artifact field is required, of
  every campaign instead of one.

  (3) THE ACCEPTANCE GATE COUNTS PER CRITERION, AGAINST THE REGISTRATION.
  acceptance_threshold_evaluated accepted a bundle recording "at least one
  pre-registered threshold actually evaluated" (:334). Its authority pins the
  record per criterion the bundle realizes and calls a bundle with an empty
  record incomplete (references/artifact-layout.md:302-306), and the graph's own
  producing node states the per-criterion duty (:2226-2229). The question now
  asks for one evaluated threshold for every criterion the acceptance
  registration records for that measurement. The denominator comes from the
  registration, never from the bundle's own list, because a producer that
  supplies its own denominator passes by naming fewer criteria - pave-spec
  9.14.1's evidence-gameability judgment, answered at its hardening rung 2, a
  check the doer does not run over evidence the doer cannot narrow. The
  registration already carries that list per criterion and already names this
  check as its reader (artifact-layout 4.5). The rationale gains one sentence
  saying so. WHY, generally: under an at-least-one floor a bundle realizing
  three criteria and evaluating one reads as a pass, and the adjudicator is then
  told to take each measured value from that bundle's evaluated-threshold record
  (agents/adjudicator.md:36) with no record for two of the three.

  THE CLAIM IN (3) MOST WORTH ATTACKING. One of the three sweep lenses refuted
  this finding: the gate is deliberately the narrow empty-record guard, and
  per-criterion completeness is caught later. Read from disk, that save fails
  three ways. stabilize_and_package_evidence's completeness activity (:2245)
  checks the bundle set against the route-scoped declared measurement list -
  per measurement, not per criterion. collection_defect_found (:2271) is settled
  by the seat that produced the bundles, which pave-spec 5.3.1 puts below the
  ladder as doer self-report; this check exists to be the read that seat does
  not perform. And the adjudicator's evidence_unstable sits after this gate, on
  the seat that has already been handed the incomplete record as its source of
  values. So this is the only independent per-criterion read on the path into the verdict.
  Provenance sharpens it: the at-least-one wording landed with revision 5
  (history/v5.patch:164), whose stated reason was that the graph had believed an
  instrument nobody had ever seen fail. An at-least-one floor leaves that same
  blind spot over the criteria a bundle silently skips, so this hunk finishes
  revision 5's own item rather than reopening it.

  (4) FIVE RESTATEMENTS COLLAPSE TO POINTERS THEY ALREADY CARRIED. In each case
  the clause that changes what the node does stays and the reference's shape
  goes. run_candidate_measurements' defect-record activity (:2158-2166) keeps
  "write every defect finding as its own event file, so the budget stays
  derivable by counting defect-record files by path - one instrument, two
  predicates" and loses the three-and-nine magnitudes and the novelty
  derivation. stabilize_and_package_evidence loses the same numbers at both its
  sites - the completeness activity (:2245-2251) and the exhaustion activity
  (:2254-2257) - and its declared_measurement_unproducible meaning (:2277-2282)
  keeps the derivation and loses the magnitudes; the outcome means exactly what
  it meant. capture_baseline_reference's purpose (:2093-2097) keeps "out of scope
  - any durable host-state mutation on the baseline, ever" and loses the
  enumeration and the lifecycle clause it reproduced in the same sentence that
  claimed the definition "lives once" elsewhere. record_changeset's purpose
  (:1670-1674) keeps "both transcripts meet the scan-completeness discipline
  pinned at references/artifact-layout.md section 4.6" and loses that section's
  three-item census and its rationale. Two vague pointers ("the consolidated
  artifact-layout entry") become numbered ones, section 4.4 and section 4.10,
  matching the style the graph already uses at :1304 and :1671; the 4.10 pointer
  also names the capture-launch boundary ruling that the deleted copy omitted, so
  the pointer is more complete than the text it replaces. WHY, generally:
  pave-spec 4.11 says remove any element whose absence does not change required
  routing, authority, evidence, recovery, or acceptance, and every clause cut
  here passes that test - a reader of these nodes now gets the one authority the
  reference itself declares single, instead of a copy that can drift from it. Two of these sites are revision 5's own text (v5.patch:235) against
  revision 5's own stated pattern, "the graph states the duty and cites the
  shape".

  THE TRADE-OFF IN (4), STATED SO IT CAN BE ATTACKED. The magnitudes and the
  census items now live only in the release layer, outside the pinned graph
  bundle, so a release can move a suggested bound without a graph revision. I
  judge that right. references/artifact-layout.md:245-247 already declares itself
  the single definition and names these two nodes as its citers, and
  agents/measurer.md:106-108 already orders the seat to cite it and not restate
  the numbers. Four graph copies did not protect the bound - they created the
  divergent normalization that rule was minted to prevent, and an amendment to
  4.4 had to find four graph sites to stay consistent. Both magnitudes are
  advisory ("suggested"), the release layer is line-ratcheted and tested, and it
  lands under the same user gate as the graph. If the lead would rather have the
  numbers inside the digest, the coherent move is the opposite one - delete them
  from 4.4 and pin them in the graph - never two homes for one bound.

  PRICE PER RUN: no new seat, node, edge, outcome, check, artifact or lap. Item 3
  changes what the lead counts at a gate it already runs: instead of finding one
  evaluated-threshold record per bundle it counts them against the criteria the
  registration already lists, a read of two persisted artifacts, on the lead
  mechanical rung. Items 1, 2 and 4 cost nothing - they remove text or correct a
  term. Against that, item 3 closes the only path by which a bundle realizing
  several criteria reaches a parity verdict with one of them evaluated, and item
  1 stops the graph from telling a measurer to build the harness that produced
  the worst measurement defect in this domain's recorded history.

  WHAT GREW AND WHAT WAS CUT. The only addition is item 3's question and
  rationale, +4 lines. Everything else is a cut: -11 lines over the six
  restatement hunks and -1 at the trap activity, for 28 added against 36 removed
  and a net -8 on a 2811-line graph. Nothing new is pinned. One note for the
  release layer, not this patch: tests/test_document_ceilings.py pins every
  README, reference, seat contract and SKILL.md, but not workflow.pave.yaml, so
  the graph is the one prose file in this package that can grow silently.

  EVERY COPY OF EVERY CLAUSE THIS PATCH TOUCHES, AND ITS DISPOSITION.
  "streaming harness": measurement-pitfalls.md:48 is the authority narrative and
  stands; workflow.pave.yaml:2048 is cut here; VERSION:29 is the append-only
  disclosure of this very defect and stands. "stock serving-benchmark": graph
  only, cut. Decode-connector clause: cut here; the one-clause applications in
  agents/measurer.md:36, its codex mirror and SKILL.md:225 stand, each already
  naming the reference. "at least one pre-registered": graph only, reworded.
  Three-and-nine magnitudes: artifact-layout.md:234 and :241 are the authority;
  all four graph copies (:2162, :2165, :2256, :2279) are cut. Durable-host-state
  enumeration: graph :2094 is cut; agents/measurer.md:57-59 and its codex mirror
  still carry it - release layer, named below. Census three-item list:
  artifact-layout.md:289 is the authority, graph :1672 is cut,
  measurement-pitfalls.md:32 still carries it - release layer, named below.
  "deepseek": graph :256 only, outside the append-only records
  (revisions.yaml:243 and history/v5.patch:10 are provenance citations and are
  never edited).

  CROSS-LAYER COUNTERPARTS FOR THE LEAD TO ROUTE, deliberately not in this
  patch because a blended patch is unreviewable. (a) agents/measurer.md:57-59
  and codex/agents/vllm_neuron_parity_measurer.toml restate the section 4.10
  durable-host-state enumeration beside their own "lives once in 4.10" pointer -
  the same defect this patch cuts from the graph, one layer over. (b)
  references/measurement-pitfalls.md:32 restates the section 4.6 census list
  (1.5.2 review-record residual 2); after this revision that pair is the last
  copy of it. (c) tests/test_document_ceilings.py could pin workflow.pave.yaml.
  None of the three blocks this revision.

  USAGE EVIDENCE (evolution contract rule 8). No usage record exists for this
  workflow: no parity run has executed against it, the root holds no usage
  ledger, and usage_evidence is therefore none, not the field this root's
  revision 5 could claim from a sibling campaign's verified learnings. What I
  read in its place: the five semantic diffs in revisions.yaml and the 1.5.2
  review record. They changed this proposal twice. Revisions 1 through 4 each cut
  priced judgment that never fired, and the one revision that added a seat added
  twenty to fifty-five dispatches per campaign, so this proposal adds no seat and
  no lap and puts its single strengthening on the lead-mechanical rung. And
  revision 5's own diff states the pattern this patch applies - the graph states
  the duty and cites the shape - which is why three sites are collapsed to
  pointers rather than reworded. Nothing in the ledger shows a measurement
  boundary seat whose priced judgment never fired, so nothing here retires one.

  DEFECT EVIDENCE, DISPOSED IN FULL. All nine graph-layer findings of the 1.5.2
  consolidation sweep are fixed and none is declined: :2047 and :2048 in item 1,
  :256 in item 2, :334 in item 3, :1671, :2093, :2161, :2256 and :2279 in item 4.
  The tenth site, :2049-2050, comes from 1.5.2 review-record residual 1 rather
  than the sweep and is fixed in item 1. Mechanical checks on the patched graph:
  validate_pave PASS at 32 nodes, 95 edges, 5 control endpoints; 42 pytest; 31
  hook checks.
envelope_check: changed_with_approval
plan_evidence: verified
usage_evidence: none
changelog_entry: >-
  Revision 6 (graph): two checks stop asking the wrong question and five node
  bodies stop restating their references. Counts are unchanged at 32 nodes, 95
  edges, 16 checks, 24 evidence definitions and 5 control endpoints; 28 added
  lines against 36 removed. realize_measurement_procedures no longer prescribes a
  streaming harness for speculative decode - the trap is chunk-derived counting in
  any harness, so the activity points at references/measurement-pitfalls.md and
  says that swapping the instrument that exposed a counting trap is not the
  remedy. kickoff_contract_approved asks for the "prior-run carry-over decisions"
  its own contract definer names, not a "deepseek carry-over decision" - the model
  name leaked in from the DeepSeek-V4-Flash sibling campaign cited as revision 5's
  provenance and made the clause unfireable on every other campaign.
  acceptance_threshold_evaluated moves from "at least one pre-registered
  threshold" to one per criterion the acceptance registration records for that
  measurement, matching the record shape pinned at artifact-layout 4.6 and the
  producing node's own text, with the denominator taken from the registration so
  the producing seat cannot narrow it. The repair-budget magnitudes (four copies),
  the durable-host-state definition and the scan-completeness census list collapse
  to numbered pointers at artifact-layout 4.4, 4.10 and 4.6, which those entries
  already declare as their single definitions. Field evidence: the 1.5.2
  consolidation sweep confirmed nine graph-layer findings with three-lens
  refutation, and the 1.5.2 release record deferred the streaming-harness and
  decode-connector clauses to this revision because a release patch cannot legally
  touch the live graph.
